{"_data": [{"contents": [{"content": "Vanessa and Marco's First Argument", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "It's Not Me, It's You", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 3, "type": "position"}, {"content": "scholar > Around the World > Jazzing it up in Montreal", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 12, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B1.1", "type": "level"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Describe  routines and regular activities in a wider range of social and work contexts.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations.", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations.", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations.", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations.", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations.", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations.", "type": "secondary_8"}], "type": "objectives"}, {"content": "engenn6le12ob03re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Expressing What is Necessary", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use <span class=\"strong\">have got to</span> to say what you or another person needs to do. <span class=\"strong\">Have got to</span> is more commonly used in British English.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":2,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Subject<br>I/they/we/you<br>She/he\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<br><span class=\\\"strong\\\">+ have got to/<br>has got to</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<br>+ verb in base form + complement.\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">You have got to</span> tone it down.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">I've got to</span> get my feelings under control.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">He's got to</span> get his feelings under control.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">She's got to</span> know what she wants.", "type": "example"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Used to and Would to Talk About Past Habits", "type": "heading"}, {"content": " ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "You talk about regular events in the past, you can use <span class=\"strong\">used to</span> or <span class=\"strong\">would</span>.<br><br> <span class=\"italic\">Example:<br> We used to think we were meant to be together.<br> We'd say we were soul mates.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You use <span class=\"strong\">used to</span> when you refer to conditions, states or actions that do not happen anymore. <br><br><span class=\"italic\">Example:<br> You used to be more fun ... what happened?<br> We used to make plans together.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You use <span class=\"strong\">would</span> for actions that were repetitive in the past. However, you do not use it to talk about past state.<br><br> <span class=\"italic\">Example:<br> In San Francisco, you would let me decide things for us.<br> We'd spend more time together.</span>", "type": "text"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": "demanding", "type": "name"}, {"content": "hard to please; tiresome", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Are you usually this demanding?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le12ob03aud01", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "These are words you use in an argument.", "type": "text"}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"content": "to phrase", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to say; to put into words", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: You should be more careful about how you phrase things.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le12ob03aud02", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "to throw someone out ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to make someone leave a place", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: You're dangerously close to me throwing you out.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le12ob03aud03", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "stubborn", "type": "name"}, {"content": "unwilling to change your mind", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: You're being very stubborn right now.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le12ob03aud04", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "to get carried away ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to be overcome with emotion ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Sometimes I get a little carried away.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le12ob03aud05", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "to get something under control", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to gain control of a situation after losing it for a short time", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I've got to get my feelings under control.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le12ob03aud06", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Write down 6 adjectives and 6 adverbs on different pieces of paper.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "With a partner, mix up the words together.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Choose a word from the pile and use that word to start a conversation.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Talk about yourself or other people.", "type": "text"}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"content": "I write down 6 adjectives and 6 adverbs.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I use these words to start a conversation with my partner.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I talk about myself and other people.", "type": "text"}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}], "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"template_override": 1, "contents": [{}], "_data": [], "id": 0, "type": "welcome"}, {"template_override": 1, "_data": [], "title": "", "type": "audio", "contents": [{"value": {"images": [{"image": "engenn6le12ob03re2img07.jpg", "time": "0", "id": 0, "text": ""}, {"image": "engenn6le12ob03re2img07.jpg", "time": "100", "id": 1, "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: So, you want a tour of my place? Are you usually this demanding?<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Marco</span>: I've got to be ... you don't know what you want.<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: You're going to have to be more careful about how you phrase things. I do know what I want, I'm just not as pushy as you. You're always telling me what to do!"}, {"image": "engenn6le12ob03re2img07.jpg", "time": "15900", "id": 2, "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Marco</span>: In San Francisco, you would let me decide things for us. You hardly ever offered your own ideas ... it was always \u201cMarco ... what should we do tonight? Marco ... what should I wear? Marco ...\u201d<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: You're dangerously close to me throwing you out ... you have got to tone it down.<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Marco</span>: You're being unreasonably stubborn right now, V. You used to be more fun ... what happened?"}, {"image": "engenn6le12ob03re2img06.jpg", "time": "42600", "id": 3, "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: Nothing happened. I don't like the way you're acting right now. <br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Marco</span>: You're right. It's not you, it's me. I've got to get my feelings under control. I'm just so passionately involved in trying to make you happy. Sometimes I get a little carried away."}], "audiosrc": "engenn6le12ob03re2aud01", "coverimg": "engenn6le12ob03re2img07.jpg"}, "type": "slideshow"}], "id": 2}, {"template_override": 1, "_data": [], "title": "", "type": "text", "contents": [{"value": "engenn6le12ob03re6aud03", "type": "audio"}], "id": 3}], "exercises": [{"template_override": 1, "_data": [{"contents": [{"content": "Vocabulary and Grammar", "type": "skill"}, {"content": "Reading", "type": "skill"}, {"content": "I can talk about people's behavior and personality.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "I can talk about  past and present habits.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "I can talk about what is necessary.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content"